From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: gen4m: log the systrace markers with pr_debug

tracing_mark_write() wrote the driver's systrace markers with
trace_printk(). Any module that contains a trace_printk() call makes the
kernel allocate the trace_printk buffers and print the "trace_printk()
being used ... unsafe for production" notice when it loads, although
the markers are off unless the TRACE debug class is set.

Use pr_debug(): the markers stay available through dynamic debug, and
the module no longer carries a trace_printk format.
---
--- a/wlan_drv_gen4m_6789/os/linux/gl_kal.c
+++ b/wlan_drv_gen4m_6789/os/linux/gl_kal.c
@@ -308,7 +308,7 @@
 
 #undef __BUFFER_SIZE
 
-	trace_printk("%s", buf);
+	pr_debug("%s", buf);
 }
 #endif
 
